From 23fb0fd8c04a63e0f0f3ccfb872c527cdf6b6c64 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 09:06:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Keep warm backends observing late update pauses

A successor can finish its boot scan while a predecessor resumes its first pause in place. If that predecessor pauses again before exiting, the empty-scan exit (or the fixed 600-second deadline) leaves no observer to adopt its durable marker. The outcome classifier correctly reports an interrupted tool tail; it is not the cause.

Keep paused-only recovery alive as passive infrastructure, backing off to 30 seconds with no eligible pauses and retaining the existing 5-second pending cadence. Normal crash recovery remains boot-only; writer, freshness, attempt, Stop and session.resume admission checks are unchanged. An optional stop event makes observer teardown explicit for fixtures.

Proof: new late-pause cases failed on the old loop at both 60s and 720s. Canonical runner: 22 consumer files, 476 passing tests; final 12-case regression passes, including opted-out, capped, stopped, ordinary-crash and shutdown controls. scripts/check --base origin/main passed.
